From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Rouesnel <wrouesnel@wrouesnel.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:34:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] rdp: Proxy URBDRC channels to rdp-usb-gw

RDP clients can redirect USB devices to the server over the URBDRC
dynamic virtual channel (MS-RDPEUSB). Implementing MS-RDPEUSB means
handling USB request blocks and making devices appear on the host, which
doesn't belong in gnome-remote-desktop.

rdp-usb-gw does that: it implements the server side of MS-RDPEUSB and
attaches redirected devices with USB/IP's vhci_hcd. It doesn't speak
RDP, and instead borrows the session's URBDRC channels over a unix
socket.

When the session's dynamic channels are ready, connect to rdp-usb-gw's
socket and open, close, and relay URBDRC channel instances as it asks.
The socket protocol is described in rdp-usb-gw's docs/protocol.md.

If the socket isn't there, carry on without USB redirection.
RDP_USB_GW_SOCKET overrides the socket path.

Backported to 46, where channels aren't GrdRdpDvc subclasses: the proxy
is a plain GObject that tears itself down through its own main context
source, like GrdRdpTelemetry, and it starts even without the graphics
pipeline.

(cherry picked from commit dc46511d5f57a6f13ef22afa4ba390f999822a00)
